{
  "summary": "This experiment tested scgpt as the RNA encoder in the RNA-only, multiprofile, avgpool setting, providing a clean single-variable comparison against both scvi_n200 (llm_summary_005, acc ~0.650) and PCA-2000 (llm_summary_003, acc ~0.591). The validation accuracy of ~0.530 (F1: ~0.515) indicates that scgpt underperformed scvi_n200 by approximately 0.12 and even the linear PCA-2000 baseline by ~0.06 in this controlled comparison, suggesting scvi_n200 remains the preferred learned RNA encoder and scgpt does not offer a competitive alternative in this configuration. It remains uncertain whether scgpt's underperformance reflects a limitation of its specific architecture or training regime on this dataset, whether it could behave differently under alternative aggregation strategies or in multimodal fusion settings, and whether other learned encoders (e.g., different latent dimensions or pretrained variants) might close the gap to scvi_n200."
}

